Causeway

Standalone desktop application for Finance Operations teams (R2R, AP, O2C) to log issues, run structured root cause analysis, track corrective actions, and generate governance reports — with no server, no cloud, and no IT infrastructure request.

Read this file fully before writing code. It encodes decisions that are already settled; do not re-litigate them mid-build.

1. Who uses this

Three personas. Screens are organised around them, not around database tables.

Agent / SME — logs an issue or near-miss and moves on. Must complete in under 60 seconds. If this flow gets slower, the whole tool fails.

Front Line Manager (FLM) — owns the RCA, assigns corrective actions, chases closure. Opens the app most mornings. Primary user.

Ops Leader — never enters data. Consumes the dashboard and generates the monthly governance pack. Uses leader mode (see §4).

2. Non-negotiables

These constraints must not be violated. If a feature request conflicts with one of these, stop and flag it rather than working around it.

No network calls. No cloud services, no telemetry, no CDN-hosted assets, no auto-update checks. All JS/CSS libraries are vendored into the repo. The app must run fully on a machine with the network cable pulled.
No concurrent writes to any single database file. See §4.
Under 60 seconds to log a Tier C issue. Measure this. It is the adoption gate.
Every write produces an audit log row. Non-negotiable for client audits.
No real client data in the repository. Build and demo against synthetic seed data only. Ever.
Taxonomy is configuration, not code. Towers, processes, cause categories and severity thresholds live in YAML. The app must redeploy to a different client account with a config swap and nothing else.
The packaged executable is the deliverable. Not python main.py. If it does not run frozen, it is not done.
